mode: "100644"
text: "# Transformation types, the honesty checklist & worked examples\n\n## Transformation types (the craft varies; the honesty doesn't)\n| Type | The reveal | Highest-risk honesty issue |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fitness / weight / health | body/photo | FTC + YMYL: typical-results, disclose aids (GLP-1/surgery), substantiation |\n| Beauty / skin / hair | photo | filters/retouching disclosure; consistent lighting; realistic timeline |\n| Business / results | numbers | survivorship, real tracked numbers, \"not typical\" if outlier |\n| Skill / progress | work samples | real timeline, don't hide the reps/setbacks |\n| Space / design makeover | photo/video | consistent framing; disclose staging |\n| Product (used vs after) | photo/demo | no misleading conditions; real usage |\n\n## The honesty checklist (run before publishing — this is the deliverable)\nBefore is real + un-staged ✓ · same angle/lighting/framing for both ✓ · real timeline shown (not implied faster) ✓\n· aids disclosed (filters/meds/surgery/pro help) ✓ · no cherry-pick / no survivorship ✓ · if not typical, actual\ntypical result disclosed (median, substantiated, clear + conspicuous) ✓ · actual consumers (or disclosed) ✓ ·\nconsent for the person's images/story ✓ · numbers real + tracked ✓ · YMYL: not-professional-advice, no\ncure/guarantee ✓.\n\n## Structure that works (before → journey → after → tie)\nHook on the reveal or the relatable before → the journey (what changed it + a real setback + the real timeline) →\nthe honest reveal (consistent conditions) → the required disclosure → the viewer takeaway. Route the video to\n`short-form-video-script`, the carousel to `carousel-writer`, the numbers to `infographic-and-data-viz`.\n\n## Worked example A — \"Blunt indie founder\" (business, honest outlier)\n\"a client went 2k → 41k followers in 6 months. real numbers, and no — this is NOT typical (most clients we've\ntracked land ~3-8k in that window; median ~5k). what actually did it wasn't a hack: 6 months of 3 posts a week,\none that flopped hard in month 2, and fixing the offer. here's the exact process.\" — real, non-survivorship,\nmedian disclosed, journey shown.\n\n## Worked example B — \"Warm bookkeeping studio\" (client, consented, no numbers game)\n\"With her okay: a client came to us 8 months behind and dreading every email. Same desk, same messy shoebox of\nreceipts — here's month 1 vs now. It wasn't magic or fast; it was one 20-minute weekly habit and a rough January.\nResults like this aren't guaranteed, but the habit is the part anyone can copy.\" — consented, honest timeline, no\ncure/guarantee, attainable takeaway.\n\n## Never\nStage/exaggerate the before · use different lighting/posing for after · imply an unrealistic timeline · hide\nfilters/meds/surgery/pro help · cherry-pick or show only survivors · say only \"results not typical\" for an\noutlier · use stock/other people's before-afters as clients · fabricate an average · post a client without\nconsent · claim WoopSocial generates the media.\n"
